# The eye moon's upper lid: the top half of a shell round the eye (12 cm), turned back about the eye's centre by 0.8 rad, so it is open
# and leaves the iris free. Turning it forward by that much about x closes it onto the lower lid: the engine does so to blink.
format 1

Material material=moon_lid
    Rotate rotation=(-0.8, 0, 0)
        Round radius=0.004
            Intersection
                Subtraction
                    Sphere radius=0.136
                    Sphere radius=0.127
                Plane normal=(0, -1, 0) height=0.004
